## Q6. When to stop reviewing

Rule: at most two rounds per slice. Round 2 reviews round-1 findings only. Land when no open finding is a P1 inside the row's scope text; every other open item goes to a known-gaps table in the design section, with slice, reviewer family, owner slice, and the claim sentence narrowed. P1 means wrong output or an unsound guard inside the row's acceptance bullets, or a regression in a landed slice; P2 is CPython parity outside the bullets or evidence weakness; P3 is style. A fix round may not add a public entry point, catalog id or frontend; a finding needing one becomes a slice. Disagreement on in-scope P1 goes to a third-family Architect, not a third engineer round. Different-family review is untouched: the reviewer still writes the "no in-scope P1" line. Lane cost: JVM only per round, three hosts once at landing, `affected.clj` for test-only fix rounds. I2's generator `__all__` and I3's profile switching would both have been ledger entries under this rule.
